ociated terms</li><li>Correlation statistics between terms before and after ChatGPT\u2019s release</li><li>Separate data tables for research articles, review papers, and case reports</li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\">This dataset also contains the results of analysing <b>12 LLM-associated terms</b> across <b>six major scholarly databases</b> (<b>Scopus, Web of Science, PubMed, PubMed Central (PMC), Dimensions, and OpenAlex)</b>  covering publications from <b>2015 to July 2025</b>. It includes:</p><ul><li></li></ul><p></p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 530036519, "created_date": "2025-09-11T09:32:51Z", "modified_date": "2025-09-11T15:56:27Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["Large Language models (LLMs)", "ChatGPT", "academic writing", "scholarly publishing practice", "AI-assisted writing"], "keywords": ["Large Language models (LLMs)", "ChatGPT", "academic writing", "scholarly publishing practice", "AI-assisted writing"], "categories": [{"id": 28864, "title": "Artificial intelligence not elsewhere classified", "parent_id": 28825, "path": "/28798/28825/28864", "source_id": "460299", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 29425, "title": "Linguistics not elsewhere classified", "parent_id": 29389, "path": "/29239/29389/29425", "source_id": "470499", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 29131, "title": "Informetrics", "parent_id": 29116, "path": "/28798/29116/29131", "source_id": "461005", "taxonomy_id": 100}], "references": [], "has_linked_file": false, "citation": "Kousha, Kayvan; Thelwall, Mike (2025). How much are LLMs changing the language of academic papers after ChatGPT? A multi-database and full text  analysis. figshare. Journal contribution. https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.30102913.v1", "related_materials": [], "is_embargoed": false, "emba